   {dialog==='editing-help'&&<div className="prose"><p><strong>Click text and type</strong></p><p>Choose Edit existing text and click a supported paragraph. Edit directly on the page; changes save automatically. Spaces and line breaks work normally. Enter adds a line, Ctrl/Command+Enter finishes editing, and Escape restores your last saved text. Download also saves pending changes.</p><p>Font size stays fixed while typing. Following words move across the line, then wrap at the available text boundary. The text area grows downward into available space. Separate paragraphs and images stay in place. If the text cannot fit, your draft remains available and the previous PDF is preserved. Decorative, outlined, overlapping or unsupported-font text may be read-only. Scans need OCR.</p><p><strong>Images, highlights and shapes</strong></p><p>Use Layers to move, resize or delete added content and supported original embedded images. Moving an original image converts it to a rectangular layer; its original clipping effects are not retained. Highlight draws a brush stroke. Shapes lets you draw, select, move, resize and delete rectangles, ellipses, lines and arrows.</p><p>OCR offers searchable output, approximate editable scans with artwork retained outside recognized regions, or an editable text-only copy. Review recognition and background changes.</p><a href="/api/sample.pdf" download="folio-sample.pdf" className="button subtle">Download editable sample PDF</a><p className="help-note">Release: smooth-editing-10</p></div>}
